%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 923d11fba433472c8bee5d08e4314b8b, type: 3}
  m_Name: Staff Database
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ComputerDatabase
  entries:
  - title: Entry requirements
    category: Rulebook
    keywords: accept deny valid passport inspection
    content: 'Accept entry only when all passport checks pass.


      1. Compare
      the passport name with the registration record.

      2. Compare its DOB with
      the record. The date must be possible and not in the future.

      3. Compare
      EXP with the inspection date: {DATE}.


      Deny entry if any check fails.
      Return the stamped passport to finish the visit. Feedback explains the result.
      Ask about baggage and apply any relevant baggage restrictions before granting
      clearance.'
  - title: Passport expiry (EXP)
    category: Rulebook
    keywords: expired expiration date today valid
    content: 'Inspection date: {DATE}.


      A passport is valid through its printed
      expiry date. An EXP equal to today is valid. An EXP earlier than today is expired.


      Read
      the month as well as the year. Dates use DD MMM YYYY, for example 16 NOV 2026.
      An impossible or unreadable date is invalid.'
  - title: Date of birth (DOB)
    category: Rulebook
    keywords: birth birthday age mismatch invalid future
    content: 'Use the registration record as your reference. The passport DOB must
      match it exactly as a calendar date.


      A different day, month or year
      is a mismatch. Impossible dates, such as 31 FEB, and dates after the inspection
      date are invalid.


      There is currently no minimum-age entry rule. Do
      not deny someone merely because they are young or old.'
  - title: Names and registration records
    category: Rulebook
    keywords: identity spelling person passenger name
    content: 'The registration record identifies the applicant and their recorded
      date of birth. Compare both with the passport.


      Names must match; capitalisation
      and extra spaces at the ends do not matter. Different letters or missing names
      are grounds for denial.


      The record remains available during dialogue.
      A friendly story does not override a document discrepancy.'
  - title: Daily checkpoint notice
    category: Notices
    keywords: company bulletin shift policy today
    content: 'STAFF NOTICE

      Inspection date: {DATE}


      Current checks:
      passport NAME, DOB and EXP.


      Read every field before stamping. Multiple
      discrepancies can occur on the same passport. The system reports all detected
      discrepancies after the documents are returned.


      Keep this terminal
      available for reference during a visit.'
  - title: 'Company notice: handling documents'
    category: Notices
    keywords: company handover desk papers stamp return
    content: 'Documents arrive in the handover area. Move the passport onto the inspection
      desk to open it and read its details.


      Stamp Accept or Deny while the
      passport is in inspection. Return it to the handover area to finish the visit.


      Next
      Person begins another visit with fresh documents. Opening the staff terminal
      does not finish or reset the current visit.'
  - title: Boarding pass and seat numbers
    category: General
    keywords: seat seating boarding ticket passenger airline
    content: 'The boarding pass shows the passenger name and assigned seat. Seat
      codes combine a row number with a letter, such as 9D.


      Seats are assigned
      to the character and remain the same throughout their visit. The pass scales
      up on the inspection desk for reading.


      Seat allocation is informational
      in the current checkpoint rules. It is not a separate reason to deny entry.'
  - title: Reading dates
    category: General
    keywords: calendar months format jan feb mar apr may jun jul aug sep oct nov
      dec
    content: 'Dates are printed as DAY MONTH YEAR.


      JAN January / FEB February
      / MAR March

      APR April / MAY May / JUN June

      JUL July / AUG August
      / SEP September

      OCT October / NOV November / DEC December


      Compare
      the year first, then the month, then the day. The inspection date appears above
      the desk and in this database.


      February never has 30 or 31 days. A
      future birth date is invalid.'
  - title: Using the staff terminal
    category: General
    keywords: search database computer help information
    content: 'Type a word or phrase and click SEARCH, or press Enter. Searches look
      through article titles, keywords and full text. All words in your query must
      appear somewhere in a matching article.


      Choose All, Rulebook, Notices
      or General to narrow the results. Use PREV and NEXT for more results, and select
      a title to read it. Scroll within a long article to read the rest.


      CLEAR
      removes your search text. CLOSE or Escape returns you to the desk. This is
      the checkpoint internal reference database.'
  - title: Tools in passenger baggage
    category: Rulebook
    keywords: tools toolkit equipment repairs mechanic cabin carry-on checked luggage
      baggage
    content: "MERIDIAN CHECKPOINT POLICY \u2014 BAGGAGE  \n\nTools must travel in
      checked baggage. A passenger carrying tools in cabin baggage must not be cleared
      through this checkpoint.  \n\nAsk whether the passenger is carrying tools and
      where they are packed. Their occupation alone does not establish what they
      are carrying.  \n\nTools in checked baggage do not prevent clearance, provided
      all other checks pass."
